<%# The delegated runs of this conversation, at the same edge as the usage row:
    both are facts about the conversation, and a reader checking what is being
    spent is asking the same question as one checking what is being run for
    them.

    Hidden when there is nothing to say (see SubagentJobs.visible?): a
    conversation that has never delegated gets no control for it, and one whose
    runs ended long ago keeps nothing but the tick on the toggle. The element
    stays in the page so the stream has somewhere to write; `hidden` is what
    takes it out of the row.

    The toggle says "subagent" in words rather than wearing a count. A number
    next to an icon is a riddle for anyone who has not opened the panel yet, and
    the count is where the runs are — one row each, newest first.

    A `<details>` like the two sheets beside it, so it opens without a script
    and its panel hangs above the row instead of off the bottom of the page.
    This one opens to the right (see `.usage-sheet-subagents`), because it sits
    at the left end of the row and a panel anchored to its right edge grew off
    the screen. What is inside is not drawn once: a run in flight changes every
    time it reaches for a tool, so the channel swaps the list in place (see
    Web#subagent_slots_markup). Only those slots are replaced while the sheet
    stays on screen, or an open panel would close under the reader's cursor. -%>
<%- hidden = !Rubot::Web::SubagentJobs.visible?(subagents) -%>
<details class="usage-sheet usage-sheet-subagents" id="subagent-sheet"<%= " hidden" if hidden %>>
  <summary class="usage-toggle" title="<%= h(I18n.t("web.subagents.title")) %>" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.subagents.title")) %>">
    <%= usage_icon(:subagent) %><span class="subagent-label"><%= h(I18n.t("web.subagents.toggle")) %></span><span class="subagent-state" id="subagent-state"><%= View.render("_subagent_state", subagents: subagents) %></span>
  </summary>

  <div class="usage-panel" role="group" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.subagents.title")) %>">
    <p class="panel-title"><%= h(I18n.t("web.subagents.title")) %></p>
    <div id="subagent-sheet-body">
      <%= View.render("_subagent_rows", subagents: subagents) %>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
